{
  "name": "retried-instances",
  "about": "Two attempts of one retried `flow:` node, and two attempts of one agent node's tool loop. Both shapes file records at the SAME instance path — grammar §9.4 reuses a key for a repeated attempt on purpose (`docs/trace.md` §8) — and both carry entries beneath them. It is the case a span id derived from the bare instance path collapses: the two `mid` spans would differ and their two `leaf` children would not, so a collector would merge two subflow attempts into one span. Every id below has to be distinct.",
